name cili
# The Collaborative Interlingual Index (ili.ttl): one language-neutral concept per meaning, each a statement of its own,
#   <i1>	a	<Concept> ;
#   	skos:definition	"(usually followed by `to') having the necessary means or skill ..."@en ;
#   	dc:source	pwn30:00001740-a .
# A concept is its definition, the content CILI gives it: its number (i1) is CILI's key of it, and the WordNet 3.0
# synset it was made from (dc:source, pwn30:00001740-a) is WordNet's key of it, both recorded nowhere. The concepts
# are the highway's interlingual index, by both keys. What a concept is said to be (a Concept, an Instance) is said of
# it, and so is the language its definition is written in.
match ili.ttl
format turtle
tier statement by \n\n

thing triple property[predicate=skos:definition]/object_list/rdf_literal/value
omit subject
content *

when predicate is a
relate property predicate to object_list
always
pair rdf_literal lang_tag

types ili "Interlingual index concept" triple
keyed ili triple subject
keyed ili triple property[predicate=dc:source]/object_list matching ^pwn30:(.*)$
